  "description": "Where does rain come from? Find out with Gizmo the robot: the sun warms water and turns some of it into invisible water vapor, cold air high up turns the vapor back into tiny drops that gather on specks of dust and make clouds, and drops that grow too heavy fall as rain. Small raindrops are round and bigger ones are shaped like a hamburger bun.\nA science explainer for kids ages 4-8, with questions to answer, things to copy, quick checks and a quiz at the end.\n\nWhere the facts come from (read Nov 19, 2026): USGS Water Science School, The Water Cycle for Kids and Are Raindrops Shaped Like Teardrops?; NOAA SciJinks, What Causes Rain?\n\nGizmo Explains makes gentle, colorful videos for little learners. New videos every day! Made with care for ages 4-8. Every fact is checked against trusted sources and every script is reviewed for kid safety before publishing.",
